cklinks","Output structure","Handling blocked sites","Process","1. Download and classify the start page","2. Download and classify list pages","3. Follow sub-subcategories (deeper navigation)","4. Select and download detail pages","5. Clean up","6. Generate navigation values"],"name_hint":"抓取 · 探查 · site"},{"path":"skills/scrape-review-schema/SKILL.md","name":"scrape-review-schema","description":"Generate an HTML review page for schema and extracted data verification","headings":["Input","Process","1. Read analysis data","2. Create temp directory","3. Copy static assets","4. Copy saved HTML pages","5. Generate data.js","6. Open in browser and wait for feedback"],"name_hint":"抓取 · 评审 · 结构"},{"path":"skills/scrape-scrapy-cloud/SKILL.md","name":"scrape-scrapy-cloud","description":"General-purpose Scrapy Cloud skill — deploy projects, schedule spiders, list/stop jobs, and view items or logs. Use when asked to deploy a project or spider to Scrapy Cloud / Zyte Cloud / Scrapinghub, schedule or run a spider remotely, manage jobs, or inspect scraped items and logs.","headings":["Rules","Input","Process","1. Locate the project root","2. Check for existing scrapinghub.yml","3. Create scrapinghub.yml","4. Deploy","5. Report success","Scheduling a job","Basic schedule","With spider arguments (`-a`)","With job-specific Scrapy settings (`-s`)","With a specific project","With units and priority","Combined example","Waiting for a job to finish","Validating job results","1. Errors and close reason"],"name_hint":"抓取 · scrapy · cloud"},{"path":"skills/scrape-spec/SKILL.md","name":"scrape-spec","description":"Expand a spec created by /scrape-define — download more pages, compare HTML variants, extract values, optional browser review","headings":["Input","Step 1: Read existing spec","Step 2: Explore the site","Detail pages → data type","Start + list pages → navigation","Navigation values (generated by explore-site)","Step 3: Determine navigation HTML variant","Step 4: Analyze detail sample and list pages in parallel","Step 4.5: Decide whether to create a list-page data type","Step 5: Choose HTML variant","Step 6: Extract values (skip if list_spec_created)","Navigation","Step 7: Optional browser review","Step 8: Apply feedback","Step 9: Finalize"],"name_hint":"抓取 · spec"},{"path":"skills/scrape-zyte-api-stats/SKILL.md","name":"scrape-zyte-api-stats","description":"Query usage stats for Zyte API requests that have already been sent, including cost, request volume, response times, status codes, filters, grouping, and pagination. Use this skill whenever answering the request requires looking up recorded Zyte API usage, spend, request counts, response times, grouped stats, or filtered stats — including projecting future spend or usage when the projection explicitly extrapolates from actual recorded usage (e.g. \"based on this month's usage so far, project month-end spend\"). Do not use it when the user asks what a spider, job, or workload might, would, or could generate — those are hypothetical estimates with no recorded data to query, even if a spider exists in the project. For a projection to qualify, the user must explicitly reference past or current recorded usage as the basis. Also do not use for dashboard setup, documentation, configuration, or account-help questions.","headings":["Wrapper","Stats API Parameters"],"name_hint":"抓取 · zyte · api · stats"},{"path":"skills/scrape-zyte-login/SKILL.md","name":"scrape-zyte-login","description":"Set up the user's Zyte account and credentials. Use when the user asks to set up, log in, sign up, or get an API key for Zyte; when ZYTE_API_KEY is missing; when a site is blocked; or before Scrapy Cloud deployment.","headings":["1. Check credentials","2. Run OAuth setup flow","3. Let user pick project and Zyte API key","4. Save selected project ID"],"name_hint":"抓取 · zyte · login"},{"path":"skills/scrape/SKILL.md","name":"scrape","description":"End-to-end web scraping workflow — from URL to working spider with web